From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 14:34:20 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] third_party: vendor freetype-sys with the openharmony-rs
 patches

Build freetype-sys from third_party/freetype-sys/freetype-sys through
`[patch.crates-io]` instead of the crates.io release. update.sh
reproduces that directory: it fetches upstream PistonDevelopers/
freetype-sys at a pinned commit, applies the patches in patches/ (the
commits of openharmony-rs/freetype-sys on top of it), fetches the
FreeType submodule, vendors libpng from upstream libpng with the
crate's own script, and keeps only the files the build uses.
`update.sh --export-patches` regenerates patches/ from a checkout of the
fork, and `update.sh --check` verifies the committed copy.

Compared with freetype-sys 0.23.0 from crates.io, this brings:
- FreeType 2.14.3 instead of a snapshot after 2.13.2, and libpng 1.6.58
  instead of 1.6.44.
- The memory-mapping unix ftsystem.c (and the Windows one) instead of
  stdio, so faces opened from a path no longer fread on every access.
- ABI fixes for FT_Get_Sfnt_LangTag and the FT_Bitmap and FT_Span
  field types, and bindings for FT_Get_Advance and FT_Get_Advances.

Validation: `third_party/freetype-sys/update.sh --check` reproduces the
committed copy, which is also file-identical to openharmony-rs/freetype-sys
at cf04f4e. `./mach check --ohos` passes. `cargo nextest run -p servo-fonts
--features bundled_freetype` passes 7/7, including
`autohinted_advances_match_loaded_advances` against the vendored FreeType
2.14.3, and the test binary links `ft_close_stream_by_munmap`, so the
memory-mapping ftsystem.c is the one in use. `./mach test-tidy` passes. Not
run on device; the same FreeType and mmap combination was measured on the
PLR-AL00 earlier (layout -6..-12% on the GenUI pages).
AI-assisted: Yes (agent session; written and tested by the agent)

Signed-off-by: Jonathan Schwender <schwenderjonathan@gmail.com>
---
 Cargo.lock | 2 --
 Cargo.toml | 6 +++++-
 2 files changed, 5 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Cargo.lock b/Cargo.lock
index f8b68eac03a..b97406aa276 100644
--- a/Cargo.lock
+++ b/Cargo.lock
@@ -2915,8 +2915,6 @@ dependencies = [
 [[package]]
 name = "freetype-sys"
 version = "0.23.0"
-source = "registry+https://github.com/rust-lang/crates.io-index"
-checksum = "eab537ce43cab850c64b4cdc390ce7e4f47f877485ddc323208e268280c308ae"
 dependencies = [
  "cc",
  "libz-sys",
diff --git a/Cargo.toml b/Cargo.toml
index 1953c51e5ee..a59cdea6850 100644
--- a/Cargo.toml
+++ b/Cargo.toml
@@ -10,7 +10,7 @@ members = [
     "tests/unit/*",
 ]
 default-members = ["ports/servoshell"]
-exclude = [".cargo", "support/crown"]
+exclude = [".cargo", "support/crown", "third_party/freetype-sys"]
 
 [workspace.package]
 version = "0.5.0"
@@ -442,6 +442,10 @@ lto = "thin"
 codegen-units = 1
 
 [patch.crates-io]
+# OpenHarmony fork with FreeType 2.14.3, mmap-backed streams and ABI fixes; see
+# third_party/freetype-sys/update.sh.
+freetype-sys = { path = "third_party/freetype-sys/freetype-sys" }
+
 # If you need to temporarily test Servo with a local fork of some upstream
 # crate, add that here. Use the form:
 #
